1951f5cd6","changed":true,"changed_paths":["instrumentation/aws-sdk/aws-sdk-1.11/library/build.gradle.kts","instrumentation/aws-sdk/aws-sdk-2.2/library/build.gradle.kts"],"commit":"3e597c69a6f92ab8b07fc791fb11b4f34adba59f","commits":[{"changed_paths":["instrumentation/aws-sdk/aws-sdk-1.11/library/build.gradle.kts","instrumentation/aws-sdk/aws-sdk-2.2/library/build.gradle.kts"],"commit":"3e597c69a6f92ab8b07fc791fb11b4f34adba59f","parent":"0436f00dd1f35b05d608262ca5197d1c385dd87d","patch_sha256":"61474546e802064495a2c3e27f21cd256eb7df5f9f54f768c9a2e4a3212b1b50","subject":"Fix AWS SDK metadata collection profile coverage","tree":"b6cb590a1f054485acd2035cbe554db32a027d1e"}],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"61474546e802064495a2c3e27f21cd256eb7df5f9f54f768c9a2e4a3212b1b50","finding_commits":{"inline:4300806011":"3e597c69a6f92ab8b07fc791fb11b4f34adba59f","inline:4300806028":"3e597c69a6f92ab8b07fc791fb11b4f34adba59f","inline:4300806045":"3e597c69a6f92ab8b07fc791fb11b4f34adba59f","review:5555442787":"3e597c69a6f92ab8b07fc791fb11b4f34adba59f"},"parent":"0436f00dd1f35b05d608262ca5197d1c385dd87d","patch_sha256":"61474546e802064495a2c3e27f21cd256eb7df5f9f54f768c9a2e4a3212b1b50","tree":"b6cb590a1f054485acd2035cbe554db32a027d1e"},"dispositions":{"findings":[{"analysis":"All three issues in the review overview are confirmed and fixed in the same collection-profile commit: both SDK logs tasks now select the inherited SQS delete-error test, and the AWS 2.2 experimental task excludes the mixed-profile isolation fixture. Fresh telemetry includes messaging.settle.exception for both SDK scopes and no test-camel scope; baseline isolation coverage is retained.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"review:5555442787"},{"analysis":"The AWS 1.11 logs task selected only S3ClientTest. AbstractSqsTracingTest.testDeleteMessageError exercises the SQS settle instrumenter, whose factory registers the messaging settle exception extractor. Added SqsTracingTest.testDeleteMessageError without removing S3 coverage. The final logs profile passed all 5 tests, and fresh events metadata contains messaging.settle.exception and rpc.client.call.exception under the existing builder-plus-logs label.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4300806011"},{"analysis":"SqsProcessMetricsIsolationTest creates telemetry with receive telemetry both enabled and disabled, omits the experimental-attributes builder setting, and asserts metrics from the synthetic test-camel scope. It therefore does not match the experimental collection label, as documented in instrumentation-docs/readme.md:41-53,61-67. Excluded only this fixture from testExperimentalAttributes. Its baseline test task still passed all 3 regression tests; the collected experimental profile contains no isolation test and fresh telemetry contains no test-camel scope.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4300806028"},{"analysis":"The AWS 2.2 logs task selected only Aws2ClientTest. Aws2SqsDefaultPropagatorTest inherits testDeleteMessageError from AbstractAws2SqsTracingTest and uses the configured telemetry builder. Added that individual method without selecting the unrelated SQS regression variants. It passed in the 68-test logs profile, and fresh events metadata contains messaging.settle.exception alongside rpc.client.call.exception under the existing builder-plus-logs label.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4300806045"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"0a2ec222ce3af4c53190fe573da6e2dbc8cbe18316e72c727a79cb71c20d9bd6","schema":2},"download_sha256":"cd26cba20151e4381a137931c3ae9e7529a131d1df880c61bf1ac5ef2f895b27","frozen_sha":"0436f00dd1f35b05d608262ca5197d1c385dd87d","pr":20649,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"0a2ec222ce3af4c53190fe573da6e2dbc8cbe18316e72c727a79cb71c20d9bd6","request_id":"05f261e2db514bfc872d3c5648165707","run_attempt":1,"run_id":38993329976,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:cd26cba20151e4381a137931c3ae9e7529a131d1df880c61bf1ac5ef2f895b27","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":38994926957},"workflow_revision":"ec547bcfe631b43c53ada4bb386c16a217cee65b"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5550480996,5552333641,5552569436,5552994741,5554798626,5554906168,5555042038,5555095325,5555420571,5555442787],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nCollection filters omit SQS exception events and include a regression fixture whose telemetry does not match its profile label.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>3 open issues</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Include SQS error test in AWS 1.11 collection profile](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20649#discussion_r4300806011) \u00b7 New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Exclude SqsProcessMetricsIsolationTest from collection variant](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20649#discussion_r4300806028) \u00b7 New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Include default-propagator SQS error test in AWS 2.2 profile](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20649#discussion_r4300806045) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5555442787","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5555442787},{"body":"[Testing] Restricting this task to `S3ClientTest` excludes the inherited `SqsTracingTest.testDeleteMessageError`, which emits `messaging.settle.exception` in logs mode. S3 exercises `rpc.client.call.exception`, and no other collected AWS 1.11 task enables exception logs, so the generated event inventory omits the SQS event. Include the SQS error test in this profile.","comment_commit_id":"0436f00dd1f35b05d608262ca5197d1c385dd87d","comment_id":4300806011,"key":"inline:4300806011","kind":"inline","line":111,"original_commit_id":"0436f00dd1f35b05d608262ca5197d1c385dd87d","original_line":111,"path":"instrumentation/aws-sdk/aws-sdk-1.11/library/build.gradle.kts","review_commit_id":"0436f00dd1f35b05d608262ca5197d1c385dd87d","review_id":5555442787,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-17T01:53:54Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"c0fa796dfda1ac81c92b9c017317e31934a692040dbb6e633e5d5722254b4307","id":4300806011,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-17T01:53:54Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86tbquf"},{"body":"[Testing] This collected profile also selects `internal.SqsProcessMetricsIsolationTest`. That regression fixture enables and disables receive telemetry independently of this task and never enables experimental attributes. Its `waitAndAssertMetrics(...)` calls therefore collect telemetry under the wrong profile label, including metrics from the synthetic `test-camel` scope. Exclude this fixture from the collection variant, as required by `instrumentation-docs/readme.md:52,64-67`; it remains covered by the baseline `test` task.","comment_commit_id":"0436f00dd1f35b05d608262ca5197d1c385dd87d","comment_id":4300806028,"key":"inline:4300806028","kind":"inline","line":94,"original_commit_id":"0436f00dd1f35b05d608262ca5197d1c385dd87d","original_line":94,"path":"instrumentation/aws-sdk/aws-sdk-2.2/library/build.gradle.kts","review_commit_id":"0436f00dd1f35b05d608262ca5197d1c385dd87d","review_id":5555442787,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-17T01:53:54Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"4136716187ebb5d028d942535f5002f29dac0285642674235156e4df4e58e396","id":4300806028,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-17T01:53:54Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86tbquo"},{"body":"[Testing] This filter excludes the inherited `Aws2SqsDefaultPropagatorTest.testDeleteMessageError` from the logs JVM. That operation emits `messaging.settle.exception`, which the selected `Aws2ClientTest` does not exercise. No other collected AWS 2.2 profile enables exception logs, so the generated event inventory omits the SQS event. Include the default-propagator SQS error test here.","comment_commit_id":"0436f00dd1f35b05d608262ca5197d1c385dd87d","comment